    <string name="close">Close</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">&app; has no accounts and no servers of its own. Your words, decks, review history and settings are stored only on this phone.\n\nGoogle Drive (optional). If you link Drive, the app saves one file, kanjilock-data.json, in a &app; folder in your own Google Drive. It uses the drive.file permission, which only lets the app see files it created itself. The file travels directly between your phone and Google over an encrypted connection. You can unlink at any time, and Delete Drive copy removes the file from Drive. &app;\'s use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements.\n\nAnkiDroid (optional). If you connect AnkiDroid, the app reads decks from AnkiDroid on this phone and sends your review answers back to it. Nothing is sent anywhere else.\n\nSpeech uses the text-to-speech engine already on your phone.\n\nUpdate check. The GitHub version of the app asks api.github.com whether a newer release exists, at most every 6 hours, and downloads the new APK only when you tap Update. GitHub sees the request like any web visit. You can turn this off in Settings.\n\nNo ads, analytics, crash reporting or tracking. Files you export or share go only where you send them.\n\nTo delete everything, clear the app\'s data or uninstall it, and use Delete Drive copy if you linked Drive.\n\nQuestions: use the developer contact on the app\'s store page.</string>
